# libretranslate
msgid "**One CI chain instead of four workflows.** The deploy workflows collapse into a single chunk chain gated by one validation job, with every variant getting its own row and rotating distro, filesystem and tor axes. Selection tokens pin deploy axes, retriggers reproduce the exact selection of the source run in every mode, and the regular line resumes where the source stopped. Fork code no longer runs with the base repository token, workflow tokens are scoped to the jobs that need them, superseded runs are force-cancelled, and a mid-run budget SIGKILL is counted as skipped rather than green. Apt call sites are bounded so a stalled mirror cannot burn a job budget."
msgstr "**Satu rantai CI bukannya empat aliran kerja.** Pemasaran kerja runtuh menjadi satu potongan rantai yang digated oleh satu pekerjaan validasi, dengan setiap varian mendapatkan baris sendiri dan distro berputar, sistem berkas dan sumbu tor. Pin token seleksi menyebarkan sumbu, pengambilan ulang pilihan yang tepat dari sumber dijalankan dalam setiap mode, dan baris reguler melanjutkan dimana sumber berhenti. Fork kode tidak lagi dijalankan dengan token repositori dasar, token workflow discoped ke pekerjaan yang membutuhkan mereka, dijalankan secara paksa - dibatalkan, dan pertengahan-run anggaran SIGKILL dihitung sebagai dilewati daripada hijau. Situs telepon Apt yang penuh sehingga cermin macet tidak dapat membakar anggaran kerja."

msgid "**One contract, three flavors.** ``laya`` serves multilingual checkpoints and preloads them at start; ``torch`` runs the GLiFormer checkpoint as published; ``onnx`` exports an int8 graph at build time and needs roughly a quarter of the memory. Every flavor answers the same ``POST /v1/systemone``, so the gateway does not know which one it asked."
msgstr ""

msgid "**One contract, three flavors.** `laya` serves multilingual checkpoints and preloads them at start; `torch` runs the GLiFormer checkpoint as published; `onnx` exports an int8 graph at build time and needs roughly a quarter of the memory. Every flavor answers the same `POST /v1/systemone`, so the gateway does not know which one it asked."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "**One file per addon.** Addon definitions live under `roles/<role>/meta/addons/`, one file per addon at `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml`. The file-root convention applies per file: the file content IS the addon spec, with no wrapping `<addon_id>:` key (the filename stem supplies the addon id); all files are collected into `applications.<role_id>.addons` keyed by `<addon_id>` (see [layout.md](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md)). The materialised path is `applications.<role_id>.addons.<addon_id>`, read via `lookup('config', application_id, 'addons.<addon_id>')`."
msgstr "**Satu file per addon.** Definisi penyesuaian hidup di bawah `roles/<role>/meta/addons/`, satu file per addon di `meta/addons/<addon_id>.yml`. konvensi file- root berlaku setiap berkas: isi berkas IS spesifikasi addon, tanpa pembungkus `<addon_id>:` kunci (nama berkas stem persediaan id addon); semua berkas dikumpulkan ke `applications.<role_id>.addons` keyed by `<addon_id>` (lihat [layout.md](../contributing/design/role/services/layout.md))Jalan yang terwujud adalah `applications.<role_id>.addons.<addon_id>`, baca via `lookup('config', application_id, 'addons.<addon_id>')`."

# libretranslate
msgid "**One instruction file for every agent.** *AGENTS.md* now holds every agent rule, and *CLAUDE.md* and *GEMINI.md* are gone. The rules they carried bind every runtime anyway, and the PR templates, scope tables, requirement documents and docs that named the old files now name *AGENTS.md*."
msgstr "**Satu berkas instruksi untuk setiap agen.** *AGENTS.md* sekarang memegang setiap aturan agen, dan *CLAUDE.md* dan *GEMINI.md* hilang. Aturan yang mereka lakukan tetap mengikat setiap waktu-jalan, dan contoh PR, tabel lingkup, persyaratan dokumen dan dokumen yang bernama berkas lama sekarang bernama *AGENTS.md*."

