# libretranslate
msgid "**The role tree is the audit.** Every fact about a role's MCP surface lives in its own `meta/services.yml`; no separate artifact duplicates it."
msgstr "**Pohon peran adalah audit.** Setiap fakta tentang peran permukaan MCP hidup di sendiri `meta/services.yml`; tidak ada artefak yang terpisah menduplikasi itu."

msgid "**The router is a LiteLLM pre-call hook, not a semantic router.** The hook summarizes the request, filters the gateway's own model list down to the routes that can serve it, and picks one. LiteLLM's built-in `auto_router` is explicitly rejected: it routes by embedding similarity to example utterances, which answers \"what is this about\" rather than \"which model can serve this\", and it pulls in the `semantic-router` extra plus an embedding backend the gateway does not otherwise need."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The router is an alias beside the default, and it fails loud.** The gateway publishes one additional `model_name` (`auto`). `LITELLM_CHAT_MODEL` and every existing alias keep resolving exactly as they do today, and a consumer opts in by naming `auto`."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "**The runtime identity differs.** act sets `ACT=true`, so `detect_gha_act()` in [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) resolves `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` where a real runner resolves `true`. Anything keyed off that fact behaves differently, and act cannot prove a fix to it either way."
msgstr "**Identitas runtime berbeda.** set aksi `ACT=true`, jadi `detect_gha_act()` in [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) memecahkan `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` dimana seorang pelari sejati menyelesaikan `true`. Apa pun yang dikucilkan fakta yang berperilaku berbeda, dan bertindak tidak dapat membuktikan memperbaiki untuk cara baik."

# libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The ``static`` seal wraps the raft root key with ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, injected as ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned ``rotatable: false``: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` then emits the ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Kunci segel adalah seluruh permainan.** The ``static`` segel membungkus kunci root rakit dengan ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, disuntikkan sebagai ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. Sebuah cadangan volume rakit adalah **tidak dapat didekripsi tanpa itu**, dan ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` tidak menutupinya - persediaan terenkripsi adalah satu-satunya rumah, jadi kembali persediaan sesuai. Hal ini terjepit ``rotatable: false``: segel statis membawa satu generasi kendur, dan pengeluaran yang setiap menyebarkan membuat setiap generasi dilewati tidak dapat dipulihkan. Putar dengan sengaja dengan mengubah nilai inventaris; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` kemudian memancarkan ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` pasangan, node membuka segel dengan kunci lama dan membungkus ke yang baru."

# libretranslate
