# libretranslate
msgid "At boot, ``files/mcp-api-token.groovy`` runs from ``init.groovy.d`` and mints an API token named ``infinito-mcp`` for the administrator account, writing the plain value to ``/var/jenkins_home/secrets/infinito-mcp.token``. ``tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` then reads that value out of the container, persists it through ``sys-token-store``, and hard-fails the deploy when the controller rejects it. ``MCP_DISCOVERED_SERVERS`` picks the token up from the store and the client roles build the header via the ``mcp_authorization`` filter."
msgstr "Pada boot, ``files/mcp-api-token.groovy`` lari dari ``init.groovy.d`` dan permen API tanda bernama ``infinito-mcp`` untuk akun administrator, menulis nilai polos untuk ``/var/jenkins_home/secrets/infinito-mcp.token``. ``tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` kemudian membaca bahwa nilai keluar dari wadah, tetap melalui ``sys-token-store``, dan keras-gagal menyebarkan ketika controller menolaknya. ``MCP_DISCOVERED_SERVERS`` mengambil token dari toko dan peran klien membangun header melalui ``mcp_authorization`` filter."

# libretranslate
msgid "At boot, `files/mcp-api-token.groovy` runs from `init.groovy.d` and mints an API token named `infinito-mcp` for the administrator account, writing the plain value to `/var/jenkins_home/secrets/infinito-mcp.token`. `tasks/utils/mcp.yml` then reads that value out of the container, persists it through `sys-token-store`, and hard-fails the deploy when the controller rejects it. `MCP_DISCOVERED_SERVERS` picks the token up from the store and the client roles build the header via the `mcp_authorization` filter."
