# libretranslate
msgid "By default — for an **untrusted** fork PR — the privileged `pull_request_target` build checks out the **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) from the base repository: the PR's changes merged onto base, with all workflow and build-orchestration scripts coming from base, never from the fork. Because `actions/checkout` otherwise refuses to fetch a PR ref under `pull_request_target`, the source checkout sets `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. The untrusted build runs **without organization secrets** — `secrets: inherit` is not passed and it authenticates to GHCR with the per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN` only, so a malicious fork cannot read repository/organization secrets. (The `pull_request_target` token still carries `packages: write`, so the `🛡️ Trusted` label remains the real trust boundary for anything beyond image publication.)"
msgstr "Secara default - untuk **tidak dipercaya** humas fork - hak istimewa `pull_request_target` membangun cek keluar **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) dari repositori dasar: perubahan PR bergabung ke dasar, dengan semua alur kerja dan skrip archestration build- berasal dari dasar, tidak pernah dari garpu. Karena `actions/checkout` jika menolak untuk mengambil PR ref di bawah `pull_request_target`, set checkout sumber `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. Bangunan tak terpercaya berjalan **tanpa rahasia organisasi** - `secrets: inherit` tidak dilewatkan dan otentikasi ke GHCR dengan per- job `GITHUB_TOKEN` hanya, jadi garpu berbahaya tidak dapat membaca rahasia repositori / organisasi. (The `pull_request_target` Token masih membawa `packages: write`, jadi `🛡️ Trusted` label tetap batas kepercayaan nyata untuk apa pun di luar publikasi gambar.)"

# libretranslate
msgid "By default, LDAP user passwords are updated on every deployment run."
