# libretranslate
msgid "For ANY non-trivial command (test runs, deploys, long pipelines), you MUST stream the FULL output to a file under `/tmp/` via `… 2>&1 | tee /tmp/<name>.log` and grep / inspect that file repeatedly instead of re-running the command. Reason: re-running `make test` to \"find the failure I just lost\" costs 2 minutes per cycle; grepping the saved log costs milliseconds."
msgstr "Untuk perintah tidak-sepele apapun (uji berjalan, menyebar, jaringan pipa panjang), Anda HARUS stream keluaran FULL ke file di bawah `/tmp/` via `… 2>&1 | tee /tmp/<name>.log` dan grep / periksa berkas itu berulang kali daripada menjalankan ulang perintah. Alasan: berjalan ulang `make test` ke \"menemukan kegagalan Aku hanya kehilangan\" biaya 2 menit per siklus; mengambil biaya log yang disimpan milidetik."

# libretranslate
msgid "For Bash specifically, the wildcard allow entry `Bash(*)` auto-allows every invocation that does not match a `deny` or `ask` rule. The legacy `sandbox.autoAllowBashIfSandboxed: true` flag remains enabled as defence-in-depth, but the `Bash(*)` entry is now the primary gate, so shell shapes the sandbox heuristic used to decline (env-prefixes, `&&`/`|` chains, quoted multi-word args, redirections) no longer need per-shape allow entries."
msgstr "Untuk Bash secara khusus, wildcard memungkinkan entri `Bash(*)` auto- memungkinkan setiap pemanggilan yang tidak cocok dengan `deny` atau `ask` aturan. Warisan `sandbox.autoAllowBashIfSandboxed: true` bendera tetap diaktifkan sebagai pertahanan -in-kedalaman, tetapi `Bash(*)` entri sekarang gerbang utama, sehingga shell bentuk sandbox heuristik digunakan untuk menurun (env- prefix, `&&`/`|` rantai, kutipan multi- word args, redireksi) tidak perlu lagi pershape memungkinkan masukan."

